<!--
    Swift metadata names on folded code (`swiftmetadata`, identical code
    folding).

    Issue: the linker folds functions with identical bodies, so one address
    is the target of several metadata records of unrelated types, and the
    pass named it after whichever record sorted first (on the Toyota iOS
    app, 2,350 of the 57,147 named functions; 2,037 of them claimed by more
    than one type) while the layout arm typed its `self` after another.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement, the Swift metadata pass
    (`kuna-analysis/src/analyzers/swift/mod.rs`, `resolve_claims`).

    P0 assertion: `option swiftmetadata on|off` (the fix needs no option
    of its own: it only corrects wrong output).

    Both passes clear the harness architecture and load the real fixture
    `swift_icf_elf` (x86-64 ELF, swiftc 6.3 with function sections and the
    linker's identical code folding, `llvm-strip` strip all). Pass 1
    (`option swiftmetadata off`) shows the placeholders. Pass 2 (on): the
    function both `Alpha` and `Beta` use for `Tagged.tag.getter` is
    `<*:icffix.Tagged>.requirement#0` with no `self` parameter; `Delta`'s
    `tag.getter` and `describe()` share one function,
    `<icffix.Delta:icffix.Tagged>.requirement#0.merged#2`, also without a
    `self`; `Gamma`'s own `key.getter` keeps its name and its typed `self`.
-->
